                        "form": "стяжа́нии"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "10117992-73cd-4c2f-b4d6-fd896aba6f21",
                        "entry_id": "7daf54eb-e14e-3136-80ca-16d26fb6ca0c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "стяжа́ниях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "efd5695b-e000-344c-b10e-7743c97a48a2",
                        "entry_id": "7daf54eb-e14e-3136-80ca-16d26fb6ca0c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "действие по значению гл. стяжать; накопление материальных ценностей, денег"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9daa09a-a7c6-4466-9004-dee87e7ed30f",
                                "sense_id": "efd5695b-e000-344c-b10e-7743c97a48a2",
                                "text": "И, несмотря на это, истинную сущность их жизни составляло стяжание, неумолчная, постоянная забота о накоплении, самая примитивная, самая некрасивая, отталкивающая жадность, с небольшим успехом прикрываемая этикетом и чопорностью."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b3070dcc-ee17-3695-888b-6fc998c9056c",
                        "entry_id": "7daf54eb-e14e-3136-80ca-16d26fb6ca0c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. имущество"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b27ac99-9009-4c2a-a449-157c43ef8bf8",
                                "sense_id": "b3070dcc-ee17-3695-888b-6fc998c9056c",
                                "text": "Умирая за копейку, по всякий день умножает свое стяжание: но притом поминутно воздыхает и говорит, что он несчастлив, что детям его останется весьма мало, что он обижен и что все бездельники счастливы, а несчастлив только он один."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9c48029b-10d1-4fda-b577-13c2c6a0973e",
                        "source_entry_id": "7daf54eb-e14e-3136-80ca-16d26fb6ca0c",
                        "target_lang_word": "gain",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "901d0b86-f429-3f62-a402-5baad218fee5",
                                        "entry_id": "69236dae-940e-3aca-b28d-28a2aea4d8df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To acquire possession of."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f67c6bc-f78b-4a78-b609-07582f616741",
                                                "sense_id": "901d0b86-f429-3f62-a402-5baad218fee5",
                                                "text": "Looks like you’ve gained a new friend."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a7f52ae-b822-4fcf-a394-eb567f4e5042",
                                                "sense_id": "901d0b86-f429-3f62-a402-5baad218fee5",
                                                "text": "What is a man profited, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a0031dd-3a87-48a9-bff3-f4aadb96144d",
                                                "sense_id": "901d0b86-f429-3f62-a402-5baad218fee5",
                                                "text": "Another answers, ‘Let him be,\n⁠He loves to make parade of pain,\n⁠That with his piping he may gain\nThe praise that comes to constancy.’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ea06a99-1558-3785-82a6-0a878a050dec",
                                        "entry_id": "69236dae-940e-3aca-b28d-28a2aea4d8df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To have or receive advantage or profit; to acquire gain; to grow rich; to advance in interest, health, or happiness; to make progress."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0a1b569-b686-483f-a6eb-84e39dacb85c",
                                                "sense_id": "5ea06a99-1558-3785-82a6-0a878a050dec",
                                                "text": "The sick man gains daily."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11314178-ed09-4b09-bc73-e74b97555724",
                                                "sense_id": "5ea06a99-1558-3785-82a6-0a878a050dec",
                                                "text": "Thou hast greedily gained of thy neighbours by extortion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa33910c-e188-37e1-bbd6-43ec5f91ce6c",
                                        "entry_id": "69236dae-940e-3aca-b28d-28a2aea4d8df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To come off winner or victor in; to be successful in; to obtain by competition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a934fe1-28b1-47f6-ab5c-f6fa71fe5a01",
                                                "sense_id": "aa33910c-e188-37e1-bbd6-43ec5f91ce6c",
                                                "text": "to gain a battle; to gain a case at law"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "298771d7-3f51-3a8b-b86d-025a0560d981",
                                        "entry_id": "69236dae-940e-3aca-b28d-28a2aea4d8df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To increase."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8616e211-c1e4-4e56-a3c8-521f458cb21d",
                                                "sense_id": "298771d7-3f51-3a8b-b86d-025a0560d981",
                                                "text": "Then they had bouts of wrestling and of cudgel play, so that every day they gained in skill and strength."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5afea2fa-bde7-34ea-a3cd-5d8dea00f658",
                                        "entry_id": "69236dae-940e-3aca-b28d-28a2aea4d8df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grow more likely to catch or overtake someone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "often",
                                            "with-on"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "022d89c2-3189-4106-a80d-87de07ad27e9",
                                                "sense_id": "5afea2fa-bde7-34ea-a3cd-5d8dea00f658",
                                                "text": "to gain ground"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af171add-c816-42dd-8cb1-5a66f8f7babe",
                                                "sense_id": "5afea2fa-bde7-34ea-a3cd-5d8dea00f658",
                                                "text": "I’m gaining (on you)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e995dcfd-9b90-3bcb-a9cd-5532a2c5e65a",
                                        "entry_id": "69236dae-940e-3aca-b28d-28a2aea4d8df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To reach."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2451341-79ea-4182-85ec-f29c4b86a83c",
                                                "sense_id": "e995dcfd-9b90-3bcb-a9cd-5532a2c5e65a",
                                                "text": "to gain the top of a mountain"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3568dcfb-913b-4951-a63f-6c41bc76b77d",
                                                "sense_id": "e995dcfd-9b90-3bcb-a9cd-5532a2c5e65a",
                                                "text": "Ernest laughed harshly and savagely when he had gained the street."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee3c10a3-8a1d-319c-980d-583f6f925b19",
                                        "entry_id": "69236dae-940e-3aca-b28d-28a2aea4d8df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To draw into any interest or party; to win to one’s side; to conciliate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b567e79c-eae9-4c24-83ed-1c4f72e6e049",
                                                "sense_id": "ee3c10a3-8a1d-319c-980d-583f6f925b19",
                                                "text": "If he shall hear thee, thou hast gained thy brother."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "367840cb-b735-4295-8ff6-36e2eadd7438",
                                                "sense_id": "ee3c10a3-8a1d-319c-980d-583f6f925b19",
                                                "text": "to gratify the queen, and gain the court"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30c64aaa-8fc8-3d18-bbfe-31a48ae1492a",
                                        "entry_id": "69236dae-940e-3aca-b28d-28a2aea4d8df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put on weight."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45845033-a329-4ad0-8666-3b59dc2c4ad9",
                                                "sense_id": "30c64aaa-8fc8-3d18-bbfe-31a48ae1492a",
                                                "text": "I’ve been gaining."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e499966c-2dfb-4ad4-9fd2-6c163a726485",
                                                "sense_id": "30c64aaa-8fc8-3d18-bbfe-31a48ae1492a",
                                                "text": "Thinspo, bonespo, meanspo, sweetspo, anything that could motivate me not to eat, not to consume, not to gain, not to fail."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e28410ef-5352-3820-aaa7-2c56e84f34e3",
                                        "entry_id": "69236dae-940e-3aca-b28d-28a2aea4d8df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To run fast."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a clock or watch"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "gain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0161f701-6b24-3f19-8580-d40ee864b6c0",
                                        "entry_id": "926ad795-6acb-38bb-990c-657eb7fcadfe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of gaining; acquisition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8cf50b6-d97c-4a60-9aff-92f170289d50",
                                                "sense_id": "0161f701-6b24-3f19-8580-d40ee864b6c0",
                                                "text": "When power is sought primarily for private gain, the social fabric decays and unravels."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d4d41d7-2e65-431e-86ec-8ddeb2be9910",
                                                "sense_id": "0161f701-6b24-3f19-8580-d40ee864b6c0",
                                                "text": "All running headlong after greedie ſpoiles:\nAnd more regarding gaine than victorie:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba759adc-8e8a-4bb5-8faa-ba5f1e4017c5",
                                                "sense_id": "0161f701-6b24-3f19-8580-d40ee864b6c0",
                                                "text": "the lust of gain, in the spirit of Cain"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31b9f53d-f86b-3b3f-9da5-668d0a14d809",
                                        "entry_id": "926ad795-6acb-38bb-990c-657eb7fcadfe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The thing or things gained."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
